   "slot": "member2_opening",
   "text": "A depeg of the paired stablecoin fits this token's mechanism because it is structurally insulated by construction, meaning exposure arises only through recomputed exit-liquidity curves rather than forced sales. When the paired asset trades at its middle target, the Member-2 headline scenario shows zero forced sales and a ratio of 0, indicating that no liquidations occur under these conditions.\n\nExit liquidity remains available across price impacts ranging from 0.5% to 5.0%, with totals varying between $7.0M and $8.9M depending on the specific depeg level. For instance, at a paired stablecoin price of 0.93 and a 2.0% price impact, exit liquidity reaches $7.7M, while deeper impacts like 5.0% push that figure to $8.6M.\n\nThese figures demonstrate that the system relies on existing pool depth to absorb shocks rather than triggering sell-side limits or bad debt events within the Member-2 headline framework.",
